Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||10-13-2001||12:40 PM||||hey everyone, anychance some one would be knid enough to give some directions as to how to replace the TC solinoid? I know it's under the side tranny pan. But all I could find out is that there is some plug that's a pita (http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011077.html)<P>other then that, I can't find much for info  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> will there be any fluid loss when I pull the cover? is it fairly straight forward? is this an afternoon thing or am I gonna be decomissioned for a few evnings?<P>-Rick||||reg||1
Z||000001||Wolfhound||10-13-2001||01:02 PM||||Rick if you car is pre 87 it's a real quick job. The 87-88 transmission mount wraps around the end cover and takes a bit more time. Here is a link with photo instructions. <A HREF="http://www.kichline.com/chuck/fiero/TCC.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.kichline.com/chuck/fiero/TCC.htm</A> <BR>Coy<BR>You will need to jack up the drivers side and there is very little fluid lose, maybe a half pint.<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 10-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||SKIDMARK||10-13-2001||10:01 PM||||Excellent link Wolf! I wasn't aware that you could get that side cover off with the transaxle in the car. There isn't much discussion on the TM-125 and it's hard to get good information on any trans for that matter.<P>------------------<BR>White '85 4cyl coupe<BR>Black '86 v-6 SE<BR>'81 CB900F Super Sport||||reg||10
